  "arc": "Hands frame the collarbones, elbows wide, weight on the character-right foot. From frame 2 they sweep down \u2014 past the ribs, across the waist at 3, low at the hips by 4 \u2014 while the weight rolls onto the character-left and the torso leans character-left to give the sweep somewhere to go.\n\nFrames 5-7 recover, and the character-left shoulder lifting at 7 already anticipates the hands going back up. That anticipation is why this one closes on itself at 1.49x, the only clean seam in the set \u2014 it loops unattended with no blending.",
